# The guide book (1.4.1). Update it along with the README's how-to-play. Keep each page short enough to fit.
weakspot.stats.guide=Guide
weakspot.guide.1.title=Welcome
weakspot.guide.1.text=Glowing circles (weak spots) appear on blocks and creatures. Hit one to dig, grow or work faster, and it moves elsewhere. You can still play as usual without them.
weakspot.guide.2.title=Mining
weakspot.guide.2.text=Hold left click to mine and a weak spot appears on the face. Aim at it while mining to hit it and dig faster. The green bar below it shows the block's remaining health.
weakspot.guide.3.title=Repairs and Milestones
weakspot.guide.3.text=Hitting weak spots while breaking blocks slowly repairs the tool in your hand. At 100, 777, 1000 and 10000 hits you get a celebration and rewards: XP and repairs.
weakspot.guide.4.title=Growing Crops
weakspot.guide.4.text=Hold right click with an empty hand on a growing crop or sapling. Each hit on its weak spot grows it a little. Sugar cane, cactus and nether wart too. The yellow bar shows growth. If it cannot grow (too dark, for example), chat tells you.
weakspot.guide.5.title=Faster Machines
weakspot.guide.5.text=Sneak with both hands empty and hold right click on a machine, such as a furnace. Keep hitting its weak spot and it runs faster. The longer your combo, the faster it gets. Redstone parts such as comparators and dispensers work too.
weakspot.guide.6.title=Animals
weakspot.guide.6.text=Hold right click with an empty hand on an animal. Hits speed up growing up, breeding cooldown, wool, eggs and villager trade restocks. Sneak for horses, villagers and the like.
weakspot.guide.7.title=Fishing
weakspot.guide.7.text=While your bobber waits in the water, a weak spot appears around it. Keep the rod in hand, aim at the spot and left click to make fish come sooner.
weakspot.guide.8.title=Bows
weakspot.guide.8.text=While drawing a bow, a weak spot appears near the crosshair. Just aim at it to draw faster. Hits after a full draw power up the arrow (up to +50%). The gauge shows the draw.
weakspot.guide.9.title=Melee
weakspot.guide.9.text=Aim at an enemy to see a weak spot on its head or body. Strike it once your attack is charged for a critical hit (1.5x). It also repairs your weapon now and then.
weakspot.guide.10.title=Combos and Sounds
weakspot.guide.10.text=Keep hitting and the hit sound climbs the scale while a combo count shows under the crosshair. It carries across kinds and ends after about 2 seconds without a hit. Big steps up to 1000 are celebrated.
weakspot.guide.11.title=Keys
weakspot.guide.11.text=%s: turn weak spots on or off (handy while building). %s: the stats screen, where you can also change hit sounds, open the settings and read this guide.
weakspot.guide.12.title=Multiplayer
weakspot.guide.12.text=Weak spots that nearby friends are hitting show as rings in another color, and you hear their hits too. Colors, shapes and volume can be changed in the settings.
